cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "NextPad"
abstract: >-
  A slim pad server in Rust that reproduces the Etherpad HTTP API so Moodle keeps
  working through the unchanged mod_etherpadlite plugin, while running a modern stack
  underneath: collaborative writing over Yjs (CRDT), the TipTap editor, a timeline built
  from snapshots, a whiteboard, and Moodle sign-in through LTI 1.3.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Steier"
    given-names: "Christian-Maximilian"
    affiliation: "ZWEK – Centre for Training and Competence Development, Hochschule Düsseldorf – University of Applied Sciences"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7946-0461"
license: EUPL-1.2
version: "0.17.2"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - etherpad
  - moodle
  - yjs
  - crdt
  - collaborative-editing
  - rust
  - lti
  - typst
  - higher-education
